/Contents (Artificial Intelligence \046 Machine Learning \055 Module 2\072 Neural Networks \046 LLMs\012\0124\056 Deep Neural Network Architectures\072\012Artificial Neural Networks consist of an input layer\054 multiple hidden layers\054 and an output layer composed of interconnected nodes \050neurons\051\056 Each connection holds a learnable weight\054 modified iteratively during training through backpropagation and gradient descent optimization algorithms\056 Activation functions such as ReLU \050Rectified Linear Unit\051\054 Sigmoid\054 and Softmax introduce non\055linear mapping capabilities\056 Specialized architectures include Convolutional Neural Networks \050CNNs\051 for image processing and Transformers for sequential text modeling\056\012\0125\056 Large Language Models and Prompting\072\012Large Language Models \050LLMs\051 are deep learning models trained on vast text corpora using self\055attention mechanisms introduced in the Transformer architecture\056 Self\055attention enables the model to dynamically evaluate contextual dependencies between words across long distances\056 LLMs operate auto\055regressively by predicting the highest probability next token\056 Techniques like Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback \050RLHF\051 align model responses with safety and utility guidelines\056)
